OriginLore (
    origin_id: "methane_breather",
    canonical_name: "Methane Breather",
    physical_description: "Native cryogenic sentient organism, biologically adapted to the methane-sea environments of the outer Sol system. Body presents as a complex multi-limbed form between 2.2 and 3.5 meters in length, with no clear vertical bias — methane breathers do not, in their environment, stand. Skin is dark and patterned with bioluminescent markings that serve as communicative display. Respiration uses dissolved methane as the primary respiratory gas; atmospheric oxygen is toxic. Methane breathers cannot survive at temperatures above approximately 100 Kelvin without active cooling. Lifespan is approximately one thousand to four thousand Earth-years for typical individuals; some elders have been documented at over five thousand.",
    cultural_traits: "The methane breathers — the Patient Ones, in their own language — have a recorded oral history that exceeds four thousand Earth-years and predates the entire human presence in the Sol system. Their culture is, by every Concordat account, the oldest continuous sentient culture currently active. The Patient Ones are organized into extended family groups of twelve to two hundred members; family decisions are made through extended deliberation that can take Earth-years for important matters. The Patient Ones do not write in any human sense; their records are preserved in oral histories that are recited by designated memory-carriers across generations. Their relationship with humans, established formally in 2168, is conducted entirely through the Concordat-administered shore stations on Mimas. The Patient Ones consider themselves the senior species in the methane-sea ecosystem and treat the relationship with humans as one of polite, formal restraint. They do not, in any Concordat record, lie. They do not, in any Concordat record, fight.",
    gameplay_strengths: "Vacuum-tolerant (lower than baseline human in human-pressure environment but functional in vacuum). Methane-environment immune (oxygen is toxic, methane is breathable). Extreme cold tolerance. Strong telepathic intra-family communication (in proximity). Substantial lifespan produces accumulated experience bonuses in skill-related actions. Strong patience-related buffs (no panic response).",
    gameplay_weaknesses: "Oxygen-toxic (TTD comparable to baseline human vacuum exposure). Cannot survive at standard human-habitable temperature (>100 K) without active cooling. Restricted gear compatibility (most human equipment is oxygen-tolerant only). Limited to methane-rich environments for sustained operations. Restricted dialog options with non-methane-breather factions (cultural barrier).",
    home_world: "Mimas methane sea (canonical primary); rare individuals occasionally visit Mimas shore stations under controlled cooling protocol.",
    notable_origins_in_corefall_universe: [
        "Multiple anonymous Patient Ones elders (no publicly recorded individual names; methane breather convention is to refer to elders only by family group)",
        "The Long Quiet Council (the Patient Ones' formal diplomatic body)",
        "The Patient Ones who consult with Voice of Many on Crystalfold-methane-breather affairs",
    ],
)
